{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>To perform all the deeds.</b> To replace the firstborn with the Levites. Know that it was a great thing and provocative to one who does not believe, to remove the firstborn from their priesthood and restore the distinction to the family of Moses alone. And all this was because of the matter of the calf, for the firstborn offered the burnt offerings and brought the peace offerings, since they alone were the priests, while the sons of Levi slew the worshippers of the calf. There is a question here and its answer is in the section of 'And Moses went' (Deuteronomy 31)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:03.178196277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}